<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16562" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστοργ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without natural affection,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστοργος ψυχήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.146
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥστοργος</span>”
				<i>the heartless one,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					2.112
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i>Lyr.Alex. Adesp.</i><i><span class="en">
				6.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. γυνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					17.43
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πρὸς τὰ ἔκγονα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Clytus
				</span></i>
			 I, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).14
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Ios</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. θάνατος</span>”
				<i>cruel,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					7.662
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.1374
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>without attraction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.926f
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστόργης</span></b>  (sic) <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				1.50
			</span></i>.</div>
